* Component Created by Javier Petrucci and Agustin Gullino
* jpetrucc@itba.edu.ar / agullino@itba.edu.ar
*
* This is the NPN BJT
*
*         C
*     |  /
*     | /
* B---|
*     | \
*     | _\|
*          E
*
*
*  /\Ic
*  |
*  |
*  |        /--------------------
*  |       /
*  |      /----------------------
*  |     /
*  |    /------------------------
*  |   /
*  |  /--------------------------
*  | /
*  |/__________________________________> Vbe
*
*
* Behaviour:
*   - Vbe is clamped to {Vbe} whenever the BE junction is forward biased,
*     and Vbc to {Vbe} whenever the BC junction is forward biased
*   - Ic = hfe * Ib   exactly, in the forward active region
*   - Vce stays near {Vsat} in saturation
*   - reverse active region works with a beta of hfe/rbeta
*
* THE DEVICE IS PASSIVE. This is the whole point of the Bct formulation
* below and it is worth stating explicitly, because it is easy to get wrong.
* A transistor can only restrict the current the external circuit offers it;
* it can never source current the circuit did not supply, and it can never
* deliver net power. Writing the collector current as a plain current-
* controlled current source (F C E Vf {hfe}) looks correct and is not: such
* a source imposes hfe*Ib regardless of Vce, so with the collector and the
* emitter shorted together it happily manufactures collector current out of
* nothing, and for Vce < 0 it pumps energy into the circuit. Bct instead is
* written as hfe*Ib multiplied by a factor that is 0 at Vce = 0 and 1 for
* Vce > {Vsat}: that makes it a non-negative conductance, so the collector
* branch always absorbs power, as a real device must.
*
* Convergence notes:
*   - The only nonlinear elements are the two junction diodes and Bct. There
*     are no divisions by a node voltage or by a branch current, and no
*     limit() or abs(), all of which have zero or undefined derivatives
*     exactly at the cutoff and saturation operating points.
*   - epsilon/revepsilon round the diode knees so the gradient stays
*     continuous.
*   - The junction capacitances break the otherwise purely algebraic
*     feedback loop in transient analysis.
*   - A stage driven deep into saturation makes Ic insensitive to Vce, so
*     the first Newton step overshoots badly and LTspice falls back to gmin
*     or source stepping. It always converges, but not on the direct
*     iteration. Raising {vk} softens the knee and helps, at the cost of a
*     less constant Vce in saturation.
*
* Vsat is NOT exactly constant in saturation, and it cannot be. A passive
* device must carry zero collector current at Vce = 0, so deep in saturation
* Vce falls as Ic falls. Real transistors behave the same way; this model
* holds Vce between roughly 0.85*{Vsat} and {Vsat} over a 100:1 range of
* overdrive, which is flatter than a real device.

.SUBCKT NPN_nice C B E PARAMS: hfe=100 Vbe=0.7 Vsat=0.3 rbeta=20 cje=2p cjc=1p droff=100G dron=10m deps=10m vk={Vsat/15}


**Base emitter junction: fixes Vbe, and its current is the base current
Vf  B  Nf  0
Dbe Nf E   Dbe_mod

**Base collector junction: an ordinary junction at the same {Vbe}. It only
**conducts in the reverse active region and when the external circuit forces
**Vce below zero. It must NOT be used to clamp Vce at {Vsat}: that would put
**its threshold at {Vbe-Vsat}, below the BE threshold, so it would win the
**base current whenever Vce is small and collapse Vbe.
Vr  B  Nr  0
Dbc Nr C   Dbc_mod

**Transport. The first term is the forward channel, the second the reverse
**one. The 0.5*(1+tanh(...)) factor is the channel modulation: 0 for
**Vce below {Vsat}, 1 above, switching over a width {vk}. Because it is
**non-negative and the current only flows when the corresponding voltage is
**positive, the branch is a passive conductance.
Bct C  E   I = hfe*I(Vf)*0.5*(1+tanh((V(C,E)-Vsat)/vk)) - (hfe/rbeta)*I(Vr)*0.5*(1+tanh((V(E,C)-Vsat)/vk))

**Junction capacitances, needed so the transport loop is not purely algebraic
Cbe B  E   {cje}
Cbc B  C   {cjc}


**Models for the diodes
.model Dbe_mod D(Ron={dron} Roff={droff} Vfwd={Vbe} epsilon={deps} revepsilon={deps})
.model Dbc_mod D(Ron={dron} Roff={droff} Vfwd={Vbe} epsilon={deps} revepsilon={deps})

.ends NPN_nice
